WEBVTT

00:01.430 --> 00:04.530
Leaving behind countless thousands of tears

00:04.530 --> 00:08.170
My thoughts travel the wilderness

00:08.170 --> 00:16.100
The wounds will heal someday,
so come, trust myself

00:21.250 --> 00:27.760
Under the scorching rays of the sun,
what thoughts cross your mind?

00:27.760 --> 00:33.700
What does your grief-stricken gaze reflect now?

00:33.700 --> 00:42.640
If I can keep from losing my way,
step by step, it should be easy

00:42.640 --> 00:47.410
Like the wind

00:47.410 --> 00:50.480
Leaving behind countless thousands of tears

00:50.480 --> 00:54.080
I travel the dawn-lit wilderness

00:54.080 --> 01:00.520
The wounds will heal someday,
so come, trust myself

01:00.520 --> 01:07.330
Don't be afraid, change is
nothing to be frightened of

01:07.330 --> 01:13.440
As long as you are yourself, I will be with you

01:13.440 --> 01:20.180
Dreaming of tranquil days

01:20.180 --> 01:27.410
The roadless journey continues

01:51.170 --> 01:56.380
I am disappointed in you, Blue-eyes.

01:56.380 --> 02:01.220
In order to capture Ellis, those in
the way ought to be disposed of first.

02:01.220 --> 02:03.680
That is our conclusion.

02:07.160 --> 02:11.430
You are hereby ordered to kill Nadie.

02:11.430 --> 02:13.630
How to accomplish this will be left to you.

02:13.630 --> 02:17.600
However, there is one
condition you must adhere to.

02:17.600 --> 02:18.870
Condition?

02:18.870 --> 02:23.830
You are to personally execute this mission.

02:29.210 --> 02:33.440
Thus, I received the order to kill Nadie.

02:43.560 --> 02:46.430
Ellis said it...

02:46.430 --> 02:48.930
She said, "Let's end this already."

02:48.930 --> 02:53.500
Let's end this already, L.A.

02:53.500 --> 02:55.700
It doesn't make sense...

02:55.700 --> 02:59.170
It doesn't make sense, right?

02:59.170 --> 03:02.940
What in the world does she want to end?

03:02.940 --> 03:06.310
We haven't even begun yet.

03:11.220 --> 03:12.620
Are you okay?

03:12.620 --> 03:15.180
Are you not feeling well somehow?

03:19.560 --> 03:21.430
I know.

03:45.950 --> 03:48.690
What do you make of this?

03:48.690 --> 03:50.790
I don't know.

03:50.790 --> 03:55.430
Don't you think it's rather artistic
for it to be his handiwork?

03:55.430 --> 03:56.930
Um...

03:56.930 --> 04:00.470
Could it be that you know
the person who made this?

04:00.470 --> 04:03.840
- You could say that.
- We don't.

04:03.840 --> 04:09.610
If you should happen to see him,
I'd like you to thank him for me.

04:09.610 --> 04:10.880
That guy?

04:10.880 --> 04:13.820
He bought all my flowers.

04:13.820 --> 04:16.440
- Really?
- Yes.

04:18.450 --> 04:20.650
Him, buy flowers, huh?

04:27.760 --> 04:30.790
I wonder what L.A.'s up to.

04:33.600 --> 04:37.740
Maybe he went crazy after the harsh
things you said to him the other day.

04:37.740 --> 04:42.510
Oh, but if a guy who's crazy
to begin with goes crazy,

04:42.510 --> 04:45.010
I guess he becomes normal.

04:45.010 --> 04:46.950
Nadie...

04:46.950 --> 04:50.280
I don't want to talk about that.

04:53.590 --> 04:55.280
Yessir.

05:28.760 --> 05:30.930
Any experience with sniping?

05:30.930 --> 05:35.400
I've received the standard
training, so I'll be fine.

05:35.400 --> 05:38.670
Even so, that was quite a while ago,

05:38.670 --> 05:41.900
so I'm sure it'll take time
for it to come back to me.

05:53.410 --> 05:57.110
Do you know why they ordered me to snipe her?

05:59.620 --> 06:03.020
I imagine it is due to our incompetence.

06:06.060 --> 06:07.800
You're wrong.

06:07.800 --> 06:11.770
Our superiors are probably suspicious of me.

06:11.770 --> 06:13.630
What do you mean?

06:13.630 --> 06:18.410
They think I may be prolonging
the capture of Ellis on purpose.

06:18.410 --> 06:20.980
They ordered me to do the sniping

06:20.980 --> 06:23.710
in order to determine
whether that's true or not.

06:40.660 --> 06:45.100
The target left the nearby village
on foot early this morning,

06:45.100 --> 06:47.120
then went into hiding.

06:55.410 --> 06:57.180
Her purpose for doing so is unknown.

06:57.180 --> 06:59.410
Will continue surveillance...

07:07.420 --> 07:09.520
Get a little closer.

07:09.520 --> 07:11.120
Yessir.

07:16.560 --> 07:18.790
Hey, wait, you!

07:23.970 --> 07:28.810
A bird? They're trying to catch
a bird with their bare hands?

07:28.810 --> 07:30.580
It appears so.

07:30.580 --> 07:32.550
Why would they be doing that?

07:37.990 --> 07:39.680
What is it?

07:53.670 --> 07:58.160
You damn miscreant! What have you done?!

07:59.940 --> 08:03.880
Since what's done is done,
go capture me another bird!

08:03.880 --> 08:06.010
If you're unable to do that,

08:06.010 --> 08:09.810
you'd better be prepared
to pay me back in cash!

08:16.120 --> 08:20.030
Isn't there a sensible adult
around that I can talk to?

08:21.800 --> 08:24.070
Y-You're!

08:24.070 --> 08:26.770
Here I was wondering who it might be...
What a coincidence.

08:26.770 --> 08:30.200
The wretched con man "Bullshit Larco."

08:30.200 --> 08:33.170
I'm surprised that you're still working.

08:34.980 --> 08:36.710
Do you actually find any these days?

08:36.710 --> 08:41.010
Folks so honest to a fault that they
fall for your old-fashioned cons?

08:52.590 --> 08:54.300
It's not coming down.

08:54.300 --> 08:56.630
Guess we have no choice but to wait.

09:04.740 --> 09:06.640
Is the situation unchanged?

09:06.640 --> 09:08.110
Yes, ma'am.

09:17.180 --> 09:19.850
I believe that may be the best position.

09:26.290 --> 09:28.660
We will wait for our chance.

09:32.200 --> 09:36.270
Come down here already, you!

09:36.270 --> 09:41.740
And you, why don't you quit
snoozing and think of something?

09:41.740 --> 09:44.080
Something? Like what?

09:44.080 --> 09:46.950
Like, how do we catch that thing?

09:46.950 --> 09:50.790
Use our hands... like this...

09:50.790 --> 09:52.720
Yeah, yeah.

09:54.060 --> 09:57.790
If only there were some good way to do this...

09:57.790 --> 10:01.300
Oh, Ellis...

10:01.300 --> 10:03.600
Give me a little.

10:03.600 --> 10:05.590
Just a little.

10:08.070 --> 10:09.970
Mm, delicious.

10:09.970 --> 10:11.910
That wasn't a little.

10:21.080 --> 10:22.880
There's movement!

10:29.920 --> 10:31.690
What is she trying to do?

10:31.690 --> 10:34.290
I don't think they eat chocolate.

10:36.400 --> 10:38.890
- Here it comes.
- No way!

10:41.940 --> 10:43.970
That's dangerous...

10:43.970 --> 10:45.670
She's come out!

10:48.210 --> 10:50.240
If I shoot now, I'll hit Ellis.

10:50.240 --> 10:51.910
To a different position.

10:59.420 --> 11:02.090
Hey! It's dangerous!

11:02.090 --> 11:03.850
Why, you!

11:07.290 --> 11:08.960
Ellis!

11:11.430 --> 11:13.270
That was scary, wasn't it?

11:13.270 --> 11:15.000
Are you hurt anywhere?

11:15.000 --> 11:16.770
I'm fine.

11:21.140 --> 11:23.780
Man, talk about frustrating.

11:23.780 --> 11:26.770
The next time it comes flying,
I'm definitely catching it!

11:30.890 --> 11:35.020
You are the one being targeted, Nadie.

11:52.240 --> 11:55.840
Cute, aren't they?

11:55.840 --> 11:58.150
These two are husband and wife.

11:58.150 --> 12:00.480
They'll be laying eggs soon.

12:00.480 --> 12:04.190
Once the chicks hatch, you'll care
for them with me, won't you?

12:04.190 --> 12:05.950
Of course.

12:15.300 --> 12:19.830
Hey, I'm begging you, come on down.

12:19.830 --> 12:22.070
I'd like to request the same thing.

12:22.070 --> 12:24.310
Oh, are you awake?

12:24.310 --> 12:26.070
I fell asleep.

12:26.070 --> 12:28.940
- So it would seem.
- What about the bird?

12:33.180 --> 12:34.950
It's so lucky...

12:34.950 --> 12:39.820
I want to try flying like a bird, too.

12:39.820 --> 12:42.890
Yeah, that might be nice.

12:42.890 --> 12:44.430
After all, if you had wings,

12:44.430 --> 12:49.020
you'd be free to go
wherever you felt like going.

12:52.000 --> 12:54.870
Free...

12:54.870 --> 12:58.400
Is there some place that you want to go, Nadie?

13:01.880 --> 13:05.780
Now that I think about it, I don't.

13:05.780 --> 13:09.920
Even to be nice, it would be hard
to call that a constructive life.

13:09.920 --> 13:12.550
But it doesn't matter where the destination is.

13:12.550 --> 13:16.260
The one thing that's a no-go is traveling alone.

13:16.260 --> 13:18.860
It's got to be with someone.

13:18.860 --> 13:21.430
Someone? Is that me?

13:21.430 --> 13:23.530
I'm not telling you, even if it kills me.

13:23.530 --> 13:25.000
Tell me.

13:25.000 --> 13:26.470
I. Don't. Want. To.

13:26.470 --> 13:28.400
Why. Not?

13:28.400 --> 13:31.110
I. Just. Don't. Want. To.

13:31.110 --> 13:37.340
I. Don't. Think. It. Would.
Hurt. For. You. To. Tell. Me.

13:37.340 --> 13:39.110
That's long!

13:47.520 --> 13:50.160
What's wrong, Nadie?

13:50.160 --> 13:53.890
I'm bored here, so give me
something to listen to.

13:53.890 --> 13:56.230
Blue-eyes...

13:56.230 --> 14:01.000
I'm not... letting you take Ellis...

14:04.570 --> 14:06.540
Talking in her sleep?

14:06.540 --> 14:08.530
Don't scare me!

14:11.180 --> 14:14.450
Huh? Did I fall asleep?

14:14.450 --> 14:16.850
Yup, you were asleep.

14:16.850 --> 14:19.190
Sorry about that.

14:19.190 --> 14:21.420
Who's Blue-eyes?

14:23.920 --> 14:26.990
You were talking about her in your sleep.

14:26.990 --> 14:30.870
You said you weren't going to let her take me.

14:30.870 --> 14:34.300
Oh, now that you mention it, I was
dreaming about something like that.

14:34.300 --> 14:38.570
Is it the person who tried
to take me the other day?

14:38.570 --> 14:41.280
- Yeah, it is.
- What kind of person is she?

14:41.280 --> 14:43.640
- You want to know?
- Yes.

14:43.640 --> 14:45.610
Then, I'll tell you.

14:45.610 --> 14:48.180
Or so I'd like to say,

14:48.180 --> 14:50.380
but I've only had business dealings with her,

14:50.380 --> 14:53.620
so I don't really know her all that well.

14:53.620 --> 14:55.260
Are you fine with that?

14:55.260 --> 14:57.490
Yes.

14:57.490 --> 15:00.360
You see, in a word, that woman...

15:00.360 --> 15:06.100
...is a machine woman, whose head
is packed full of gears and cogs.

15:06.100 --> 15:08.500
I'm sure she's smart, but how do I put this...

15:08.500 --> 15:12.370
I think she's the type who won't
find happiness to the day she dies.

15:12.370 --> 15:14.340
How nice of you to say so.

15:14.340 --> 15:17.110
On top of which, she's underhanded.

15:17.110 --> 15:20.610
Remember? She shut down my bank account.

15:20.610 --> 15:25.520
Knowing her kind, I'll bet
she's got few friends.

15:25.520 --> 15:27.660
She's starting to seriously piss me off.

15:27.660 --> 15:29.620
You're really not holding back.

15:29.620 --> 15:31.490
It can't be helped.

15:31.490 --> 15:35.160
I mean, the worlds we live in are too different.

15:35.160 --> 15:38.670
She's a woman of the organization
through and through,

15:38.670 --> 15:44.070
and I'm a free-spirited bounty hunter,
who knows not what tomorrow holds.

15:44.070 --> 15:45.700
Free...

15:49.140 --> 15:51.670
Then you're a bird.

15:57.420 --> 15:59.080
Here it comes.

16:11.000 --> 16:13.970
- Ellis, you go around from the front.
- Yessir.

16:13.970 --> 16:15.460
Here we go.

16:22.080 --> 16:25.180
It's exactly as you say, Nadie.

16:25.180 --> 16:28.480
I'm nothing more than a small cog.

16:30.120 --> 16:32.450
But you're wrong.

16:32.450 --> 16:34.490
Even though I'm a member of the organization,

16:34.490 --> 16:37.620
I have a wish that I want to make come true.

16:37.620 --> 16:39.290
There is a place...

16:39.290 --> 16:42.090
...that I wish to arrive at someday.

16:44.770 --> 16:49.570
Freedom isn't a privilege that's
been granted to just you people.

16:56.510 --> 17:00.000
Hey, does it feel good to fly?

17:02.020 --> 17:03.280
Now!

17:03.280 --> 17:06.090
- Ellis, hold down its wings!
- Yessir.

17:06.090 --> 17:09.720
All right, we're not going to do
anything to you, so don't worry.

17:09.720 --> 17:13.490
Yes, that's right, that's a good boy.
You're a good boy.

17:13.490 --> 17:15.360
Move aside, Ellis!

17:15.360 --> 17:17.660
Please, get further away!

17:17.660 --> 17:21.500
Now, we won't have to pay that old man.

17:21.500 --> 17:23.300
Thank goodness!

17:29.580 --> 17:31.270
Ellis?

17:36.550 --> 17:39.180
Hey... Wait, what are you doing?!

17:56.570 --> 17:58.370
Hurry.

18:04.810 --> 18:06.780
Fly...

18:06.780 --> 18:09.180
Fly.

18:09.180 --> 18:10.740
Fly!

18:20.730 --> 18:22.590
Now is your chance.

19:05.870 --> 19:07.860
Blue-eyes...

19:50.950 --> 19:53.480
I made up my mind.

20:02.700 --> 20:07.530
I am... a descendant of witches.

20:07.530 --> 20:09.440
And unlike Ellis,

20:09.440 --> 20:13.840
I'm not an artificial life form
created through genetic engineering.

20:13.840 --> 20:15.830
I am a real witch.

20:18.550 --> 20:22.450
But crucially, I'm unable to use the powers.

20:22.450 --> 20:27.390
Did I have no powers to begin with,
or are they merely lying dormant?

20:27.390 --> 20:29.660
I don't even know which it is.

20:29.660 --> 20:32.830
If by arriving at that place,

20:32.830 --> 20:36.000
Ellis is able to attain her
ultimate awakened state,

20:36.000 --> 20:40.230
the probability that the same
might happen for me is not zero.

20:40.230 --> 20:44.000
Then, you never intended to
capture Ellis from the start...

20:44.000 --> 20:46.570
I wasn't sure at first.

20:46.570 --> 20:47.980
No...

20:47.980 --> 20:51.580
I wasn't sure this whole
time until just earlier.

20:51.580 --> 20:53.450
But I've made up my mind now.

20:53.450 --> 20:58.650
That I'm going to follow my
own path, just like those girls.

20:58.650 --> 21:01.960
If you do that, your life will be...

21:01.960 --> 21:06.720
That's why I can't drag you into this.

21:15.340 --> 21:17.360
Thank you for everything until today.

21:28.420 --> 21:31.690
To think we'd been tricked by that old man...

21:31.690 --> 21:35.320
Thinking about it still pisses me off.

21:35.320 --> 21:37.690
The Blue-eyes person...

21:41.030 --> 21:43.360
She had pretty eyes.

21:53.670 --> 21:56.510
Are you sure you didn't let them escape?

21:56.510 --> 21:59.080
Me? I would never.

21:59.080 --> 22:02.050
You're right. Of course not.

22:09.060 --> 22:12.030
Do you want us to come get you?

22:12.030 --> 22:15.930
But it is too late now.

22:15.930 --> 22:18.760
You are the ones who left, after all.

22:24.370 --> 22:30.680
In the end, caged birds can only live...

22:30.680 --> 22:32.670
...within cages.

22:36.550 --> 22:40.350
Like a neverending summer

22:40.350 --> 22:43.790
Like flowers that never die

22:43.790 --> 22:47.690
Those arms you've wrapped around me

22:47.690 --> 22:55.830
Don't ever let go of me

23:02.040 --> 23:05.650
Even if I try clinging to you

23:05.650 --> 23:11.450
My heart still heeds a different evanescence

23:11.450 --> 23:15.420
Counting the rhythm of time by it

23:15.420 --> 23:19.530
A night of red stars

23:19.530 --> 23:23.530
The vanishing warmth

23:23.530 --> 23:27.470
I want to keep it here

23:27.470 --> 23:33.870
You, with your eyes closed

23:33.870 --> 23:37.840
Yearning over and over

23:37.840 --> 23:41.180
Even if I can't go anywhere

23:41.180 --> 23:45.420
When the heartache comes to a stop

23:45.420 --> 23:51.730
To the two of us, this moment is...

23:51.730 --> 23:56.720
...everything
